<title>MEXICO: Mexican beer exports rise 17.8 pct in Q1 - INEGI.</title>
<headline>Mexican beer exports rise 17.8 pct in Q1 - INEGI.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>In the first quarter of 1997, Mexican beer exports totaled $94.1 million, up 17.8 percent over the same period a year earlier, the National Statistics Institute (INEGI) said on Monday.</p>
<p>Mexico's two brewing giants -- Grupo Modelo and Femsa-Cerveza -- exported $26.7 million in January, $32.2 million in February and $35.2 million in March. INEGI said the beer exports are the highest levels recorded for the first quarter period in the last 10 years.</p>
<p>((Tomas de la Rosa, Meexico newsroom +525 728-7912))</p>
